WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:04.760
Sonia Samagh, MBA 2011: "My name is Sonia
Samagh, and I am a student here at the GSB.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.450
I've completed three years of Medical school
and I'm here at the GSB to complete two years

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:15.090
of my MBA. My interest in medicine stems from
the values that my parents instilled within

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:21.039
me. As a member of the Sikh faith, the idea
of Seva and selfless service drew me towards

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:25.200
a profession like medicine.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:35.329
My interest in global health was really sparked
by this idea of health and innovation. I teamed

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:39.230
up with the professor who led the course.
Essentially what he did is he brought in surgeons

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.739
from around the world to tell us about all
the amazing things that they were doing, either

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:47.039
leper colonies in India or cataract surgery
in Africa...and I thought to myself "this

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:51.430
is something I absolutely want to do, too."
And so he and I organized our first trip to

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:58.179
Mexico, where we helped another group of surgeons
treat cleft lip and palate and burn victims.

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:01.450
With this professor, I started the non-profit
Global Health Volunteers.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:08.479
In founding Global Health Volunteers and going
to medical school, I've realized that my long-term

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:15.159
goal is to become CEO of a non-profit in international
health and medicine. In order to run an organization

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:21.409
effectively, I needed a tool set to do so...more
importantly a business school tool set that

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:28.729
the Stanford GSB in particular cultivates
in its leaders. We're on the campus that has

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:31.799
so many different disciplines, so for me coming
in as a MD/MBA student there are a lot of

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:37.979
opportunities to combine my medicine background
and a new business skill set. The motto of

00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:42.510
the Stanford Business School is "change lives,
change organizations, change the world." And

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.969
I realized that that's what I wanted to do
with Global Health Volunteers and coming to

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:51.090
Stanford will really give me the toolkit to
be able to become an effective leader. To

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.679
create an organization that really did change
lives, and change the world in the area of

00:01:54.679 --> 00:01:55.810
international health and medicine."

